       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day, depending on the formulation and label.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg in one dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 850 to 1,000 mg per dose for immediate-release metformin.\n- **Risk:** A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould you check which of these you meant?\n- **500 mg** three times daily (1,500 mg/day)\n- **850 mg** three times daily (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg per day** in total, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- A different dose altogether\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm that and give the reason. I'll enter the order once you've clarified."
